@startuml sequence_diagram_viewer_lifecycle
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title Sequence Diagram - VIS01 Viewer Lifecycle (resize, reload, leaving the page / logout)

actor User as "Restaurant Staff /\nLaPrizza Manager"
participant Shell as "AppShell / routes\n(WEB01 / WEB02 / WEB03)"
participant Auth as "AuthProvider"
participant Viewer as "KitchenViewer"
participant Load as "kitchenViewerLoader\n+ SceneAssetLoader"
participant Engine as "ViewerEngine"
participant Modules as "SceneModule[]"
participant Three as "three\n(WebGLRenderer)"

note over User, Three
    Precondition: state "ready" (sequence_diagram_open_viewer, step 5).
    One KitchenViewer owns at most one ViewerEngine. Every path that leaves or replaces the scene
    goes through ViewerEngine.dispose(), so GPU memory is released and no render loop keeps running.
    The effect creates a fresh canvas after loading assets. Cleanup removes it explicitly.
end note

== 1. Resize (window resized, navigation collapsed - WEB02 responsive layout) ==

User -> Shell : resizes the window / toggles the navigation
Shell --> Engine : ResizeObserver callback(width, height)
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : camera.aspect = width / height;\nupdateProjectionMatrix()
Engine -> Three : setSize(width, height, false)
deactivate Engine
note right of Engine : the canvas fills the main content area;\nheader and navigation are never covered

== 2. Reload (viewer "Reload" / "Retry", or "Open / reload the kitchen viewer" after an activation in WEB06) ==

alt From the WEB06 page (usWEB06 D9)
    User -> Shell : "Open / reload the kitchen viewer"
    Shell -> Viewer : navigate to /kitchen/viewer -> fresh mount\n(full sequence_diagram_open_viewer)
else Inside the viewer
    User -> Viewer : Reload / Retry
    activate Viewer
    Viewer -> Viewer : restart() calls the previous cleanup;\nabort its controller
    Viewer -> Engine : dispose()
    activate Engine
    Engine -> Three : setAnimationLoop(null)
    loop every registered module (reverse order, each in try/catch)
        Engine -> Modules : dispose()
    end
    Engine -> Engine : traverse scene; loadedAssets.dispose()
    Engine -> Three : renderer.dispose(); forceContextLoss()
    note right of Engine : if build() is pending, the attempt signal is aborted;\nthe load finalizer sweeps again when the build settles
    deactivate Engine
    Viewer -> Viewer : release assets still held by the effect;\ncanvas.remove(); set loading; increment attempt
    Viewer --> User : state "loading" (previous scene removed)
    Viewer -> Load : WebGL check; loadActiveKitchen(...)\nthen preloadAll(...)
    activate Load
    Load --> Viewer : ViewerState / LoadedAssets
    deactivate Load
    alt all assets loaded
        Viewer -> Viewer : createElement("canvas"); append to viewport
        Viewer -> Engine : ViewerEngine.create(newCanvas, ...);\nawait load(...); start()
        Viewer --> User : scene of the CURRENT active configuration
        note right of Viewer : a failure here follows\nsequence_diagram_engine_failure
    else empty / invalid / denied / expired / error
        Viewer --> User : same handling as sequence_diagram_open_viewer (C1-D1)
        note right of Viewer : a failed reload never brings back the\nprevious scene (usWEB06 3.4.5 step 6)
    end
    deactivate Viewer
end

== 3. Leaving the viewer (another section) or logout / session ended by WEB03 ==

alt Navigation to another section
    User -> Shell : selects another menu option
else Logout (AA04)
    User -> Shell : "Sign out"
    Shell -> Auth : logout()
    activate Auth
    Auth --> Shell : guest (token discarded)
    deactivate Auth
else Session ended by WEB03 after a 401 of any business request
    Auth --> Shell : guest; redirect /login?returnTo
end

Shell -> Viewer : unmount (route no longer rendered)
activate Viewer
Viewer -> Viewer : abort the effect's controller
Viewer -> Engine : engine?.dispose()
activate Engine
Engine -> Engine : mark disposed; running = false
Engine -> Three : setAnimationLoop(null)
Engine -> Engine : resizeObserver.disconnect(); remove listeners
Engine -> Modules : dispose() for every registered module\n(reverse order, each in try/catch)
Engine -> Engine : traverse scene; loadedAssets.dispose()
Engine -> Three : renderer.dispose(); forceContextLoss()
deactivate Engine
Viewer -> Viewer : release assets still held by the effect;\ncanvas.remove()
deactivate Viewer
Shell --> User : new section / sign-in screen
note right of Shell : Back navigation after logout goes through the\nmodule slot again: no scene is shown to a Guest (AA04)

@enduml
